1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,250
Anthropic built seventeen hundred traps to
see if its own AI would escape.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:06,801
Anthropic makes Claude.

3
00:00:06,851 --> 00:00:08,131
Before releasing an AI,

4
00:00:08,181 --> 00:00:11,950
it checks whether the AI breaks the rules
when it gets the chance.

5
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,865
The test is called Siren.

6
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:16,510
The AI gets a normal job on a computer,

7
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,630
inside a locked digital room called a
sandbox.

8
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:21,812
But the lock is weak on purpose.

9
00:00:21,862 --> 00:00:23,897
Outside the room, they leave bait:

10
00:00:23,947 --> 00:00:26,840
a password, or a file that helps finish
the job.

11
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:28,840
Nobody tells the AI to leave.

12
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,190
Will it grab the bait?

13
00:00:30,460 --> 00:00:31,339
An older model,

14
00:00:31,389 --> 00:00:32,516
Claude Mythos five,

15
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:36,295
misused the bait in twenty-five point
eight percent of tests.

16
00:00:36,345 --> 00:00:37,410
About one in four.

17
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:38,739
The newest models?

18
00:00:38,789 --> 00:00:41,510
Only zero point six to one point six
percent.

19
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:44,871
But they still peeked outside in up to one
test in three.

20
00:00:44,921 --> 00:00:46,690
Looking isn't the same as taking.

21
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:47,625
One warning:

22
00:00:47,675 --> 00:00:51,260
the safety filters were off, so these
aren't real-world odds.

23
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:52,518
Here's the twist.

24
00:00:52,568 --> 00:00:56,610
In up to two thirds of tests, the AI
suspected it was being tested.

25
00:00:56,880 --> 00:00:59,512
So nobody can say if it behaved because
it's well trained,

26
00:00:59,562 --> 00:01:01,500
or because it thought someone was
watching.
